.TH ping 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
ping \- send ICMP echo requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ping
[\fB\-c\fI count\fR] \fIaddress\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ping
sends ICMP echo requests to
.I address
and prints each reply with its round-trip time, then a summary of how
many were sent and how many came back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " count"
Send
.I count
requests and stop.  Without it,
.B ping
runs until interrupted, and prints the same summary then.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# ping -c 4 8.8.8.8
# ping 192.168.1.254
.fi
.SH NOTES
The radio must be up; see
.BR wifi (1).
.PP
A reply is proof the network works as far as IP.  A name that will not
resolve is a different problem \- try
.BR dig (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wifi (1),
.BR dig (1),
.BR htget (1)
